To make the BASIC programs work properly with BASICA or GWBASIC, you must
follow the examples below!!!!

BASICA EXAMPLES:

BASICA SPLIT16 /S:512 /F:3		NOTE: /S: means to use variable length
BASICA SPLIT32 /S:512 /F:5		files and use 512 byte buffers.
BASICA INTR16 /S:512 /F:3		The /F: means allow either 3 or 5 file
BASICA INTR32 /S:512 /F:5		buffers to be open at the same time.

GWBASIC SPLIT16 /S:512 /F:3		NOTE: /S: means to use variable length
GWBASIC SPLIT32 /S:512 /F:5		files and use 512 byte buffers.
GWBASIC INTR16 /S:512 /F:3		The /F: means allow either 3 or 5 file
GWBASIC INTR32 /S:512 /F:5		buffers to be open at the same time.

QuickBasic

C>QB split16 /X/O;		NOTE: make stand alone object file
C>LINK split16;			Link stand alone object to EXE file

usage:
C>split16 ofn1 ofn2 ifn		ofn1=8 bit low byte file output by split16
				ofn2=8 bit high byte file output by split16
				ifn =16 bit combined file input by split16 
C>QB split32 /x/o;
C>link split32;

Usage:
C>split32 ofn1 ofn2 ofn3 ofn4 ifn	ofn1= 8 bit low byte file output
 					ofn2= 8 bit low middle byte file output
					ofn3= 8 bit high mid byte file output 
					ofn4= 8 bit high byte file output 
					ifn =32 bit combined file for input 
C>QB intr16 /x/o;
C>link intr16;

Usage:
C>intr16 ifn1 ifn2 ofn		ifn1 = 8 bit low byte file for input by intr16
				ifn2 = 8 bit high byte file for input by intr16
				ofn  =16 bit combined file for output by intr16
C>QB intr32 /x/o;
C>link intr32;

Usage:
C>intr32 ifn1 ifn2 ifn3 ifn4 ofn	ifn1 = 8 bit low byte file for input
					ifn2 = 8 bit low mid byte file for input
					ifn3 = 8 bit high mid file for input 
					ifn4 = 8 bit high byte file for input
					ofn  =32 bit combined file for output
